course: dictionary
lesson: 14397
title: Outlaws and banned things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Outlaw can be a noun or a verb, so check the context to see which one it is. As a noun, an outlaw is a person who has broken the law and is running away from it. «The outlaw hid in the forest, and the sheriff could not find him.» The words hid and could not find him are clues that the outlaw is running from the law.
explain: As a verb, to outlaw something means to make it against the law, or to ban it. «The government wants to outlaw plastic bags that harm the sea.» Here outlaw is an action word. It turns something into a thing that is not allowed.
explain: Use the swap check. In «The government wants to ban plastic bags that harm the sea», ban fits the sentence and keeps its meaning, so outlaw means ban here. Always test your meaning in the sentence before you decide.
fact: «Outlaw» as a noun means a person who has broken the law and runs away from it.
fact: «Outlaw» as a verb means to make something against the law, or to ban it.
fact: Outlaws often appear in old stories, such as Robin Hood and the bandits of the Wild West.
fact: «Outlawed» means was made illegal, so a banned thing has been outlawed.
fact: Phrases to know: an outlaw band, outlaw a practice, be outlawed.
exercise: «The outlaw hid in the forest, and the sheriff could not find him.» What is an outlaw? | A tree that grows very tall | *A person who has broken the law and is running away from it | A kind king who rules the forest | A horse that runs very fast
exercise: The town council wants to outlaw dropping litter in the park. What does outlaw mean here? | To give a prize for | To plant new flowers | *To make it against the law | To cut down the trees
exercise: Find and copy the word for a person who has broken the law: «The old story tells of a clever outlaw.» | tells | story | *outlaw | clever
test: «Many countries outlaw cruel traps for animals.» What does outlaw mean here? | To catch | To sell cheaply | *To ban, to make illegal | To paint
test: «The sheriff chased the outlaw through the town.» In this sentence, is outlaw a person or an action? | A type of food | A kind of horse | An action, to ban something | *A person who has broken the law
exam: «The bandits were outlaws who robbed travellers, but the new law will outlaw such robbery.» What does outlaw mean in the second part? | A person who runs from the law | A town in the desert | *To make illegal | A kind of tree
